### Copilot Issue Assignment API v2 — examples
### Use with the VS Code REST Client extension or JetBrains HTTP Client.

@host = http://localhost:8000
@org  = acme
@repo = payments-service

### --- Health -----------------------------------------------------------
GET {{host}}/health
Accept: application/json


### --- 1. Create issue (no Copilot) ------------------------------------
POST {{host}}/repos/{{org}}/{{repo}}/issues
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Add idempotency keys to /v1/payments",
  "prompt": "## User story\nAs a merchant, I want POST /v1/payments to accept an idempotency key so that retried requests don't double-charge.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- Header `Idempotency-Key` is honoured for 24h.\n- Concurrent duplicate requests return the same response without re-executing the side effect.\n- Documented in OpenAPI.",
  "labels": ["enhancement", "api"],
  "skills": [
    { "name": "code-generation", "version": "1.4.0" },
    { "name": "test-generation" },
    { "name": "doc-authoring" }
  ],
  "tools": [
    { "name": "github", "type": "builtin" }
  ],
  "knowledge_refs": [
    { "kind": "repo_path", "value": "docs/adr/0007-idempotency.md" },
    { "kind": "repo_path", "value": "docs/api/openapi.yaml" }
  ]
}


### --- 2. Assign existing issue to Copilot + backend-agent --------------
# Replace 42 with a real issue number created above.
POST {{host}}/repos/{{org}}/{{repo}}/issues/42/assign-copilot
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "agent": {
    "target_repo": "{{org}}/{{repo}}",
    "base_branch": "main",
    "custom_instructions": "Follow the team's idempotency ADR (docs/adr/0007).",
    "custom_agent": "backend-agent"
  },
  "keep_existing_assignees": true
}


### --- 3. Create + assign in one call (recommended) --------------------
POST {{host}}/repos/{{org}}/{{repo}}/issues/create-and-assign
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Add NewRelic SLO dashboard for /v1/payments",
  "prompt": "Create a NewRelic dashboard tracking p99 latency, error rate, and Apdex for the /v1/payments endpoint, and document the SLOs.",
  "labels": ["observability"],
  "skills": [
    { "name": "observability" },
    { "name": "doc-authoring" }
  ],
  "tools": [
    { "name": "newrelic", "type": "mcp" }
  ],
  "knowledge_refs": [
    { "kind": "repo_path", "value": "docs/observability/slos.md" }
  ],
  "agent": {
    "custom_agent": "observability-agent",
    "base_branch": "main",
    "custom_instructions": "Pin the dashboard to the 'Payments' folder."
  }
}


### --- 4. Replace assignees (Copilot only, no humans) ------------------
POST {{host}}/repos/{{org}}/{{repo}}/issues/42/assign-copilot
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "agent": { "custom_agent": "qa-agent" },
  "keep_existing_assignees": false
}


### --- 5. List repo-level agents ---------------------------------------
GET {{host}}/agents/repo/{{org}}/{{repo}}


### --- 6. List org-level agents (from <org>/.github-private) -----------
GET {{host}}/agents/org/{{org}}


### --- 7. List enterprise-level agents ---------------------------------
GET {{host}}/agents/enterprise/acme-enterprise-admin


### --- 8. List ALL agents in resolution order --------------------------
GET {{host}}/agents/{{org}}/{{repo}}/all
